WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:02.100
Well, Andy, I mentioned
this earlier this week,

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:06.190
but let's face it, you and I
are pretty big trivia buffs.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:08.940
Yeah, we played a trivia
game earlier this week,

00:00:08.940 --> 00:00:09.773
it was fun.

00:00:09.773 --> 00:00:10.606
We sure did.

00:00:10.606 --> 00:00:11.690
Now, the first time we played,

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:13.250
your questions were a little intense,

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.320
I just wanna make sure
this time you understand

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:19.253
it's just a friendly, simple
trivia competition, okay?

00:00:19.253 --> 00:00:21.290
(chuckling) Conan, I already told you

00:00:21.290 --> 00:00:24.460
there is nothing friendly about trivia.

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.710
Whatever, let's go, Richter.

00:00:26.710 --> 00:00:28.823
All right, let's do it.

00:00:28.823 --> 00:00:31.823
(suspenseful music)

00:00:35.170 --> 00:00:37.280
All right, here it goes.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:38.550
Who had the starring role

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:43.530
in the 2014 sci-fi adventure
movie "Interstellar"?

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:45.510
Matthew McConaughey.

00:00:45.510 --> 00:00:46.600
Correct.

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:48.630
All right, all right,
all right. (chuckling)

00:00:48.630 --> 00:00:50.553
You and your spot-on impressions.

00:00:50.553 --> 00:00:51.910
Thank you, thank you.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:53.410
Classic.
All right, my turn.

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:54.400
(clearing throat) You ready?

00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:55.233
[Conan] Yep.

00:00:56.270 --> 00:01:00.010
The RMS Lusitania was a
British ocean liner launched

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.680
in 1906 that made many
transatlantic crossings

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:07.080
before it was torpedoed
and sunk by a German U-boat

00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:08.280
during World War I.

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:11.490
Okay, actually I know quite
a bit about World War I,

00:01:11.490 --> 00:01:12.640
I'm a history fan, so--

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.090
What are the current longitude
and latitude coordinates

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:18.593
of the RMS Lusitania shipwreck?

00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.210
Andy, that's like, just like last time,

00:01:22.210 --> 00:01:24.880
that, no one knows the
answer to that question.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:26.800
It's way too complicated.

00:01:26.800 --> 00:01:28.180
They're just coordinates, Conan.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:31.580
I mean, don't you know
how the ocean works?

00:01:31.580 --> 00:01:32.840
I know how the ocean works,

00:01:32.840 --> 00:01:34.453
just give me a simple question.

00:01:35.360 --> 00:01:37.973
All right, here you go, easy peasy.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:40.100
What color--

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.640
Ah, so far, so good.

00:01:42.640 --> 00:01:43.590
Was the building

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:46.500
that served New Zealand's
first cable tramway line

00:01:46.500 --> 00:01:48.240
that opened in 1881?

00:01:48.240 --> 00:01:50.170
Oh, Andy, come on.

00:01:50.170 --> 00:01:52.350
It's called trivia 'cause
the questions are supposed

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:54.800
to be trivial, simple, fun.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:58.393
Oh my God, okay, I'll give
you a real simple one.

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:03.770
Which 5G carrier is fast,
reliable, and secure?

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:06.499
Why, that's AT&amp;T 5G.

00:02:06.499 --> 00:02:08.740
(chuckling) That's right, Conan.

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.520
It's not complicated.

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:14.260
Indeed, AT&amp;T 5G is a no-brainer.

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:15.630
It's not complicated.

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:17.400
It's a no-brainer.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.770
It's not complicated.

00:02:18.770 --> 00:02:20.598
It's a no-brainer.

00:02:20.598 --> 00:02:22.848
(laughing)

